PS5 VRR: clean switching (muted while the chip switches over), all modes  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

Gilles, 1.6.2 on an LG C4: VRR works at 4K60, 1080p120, and with vrr_any_mode=1 also at
1440p60 (negative vsync, timing SDP sent anyway) and 1440p120. The only issue: the
picture drifts and flickers for the few seconds the chip takes to switch to follow mode.
 - the unmute at the end of the setup waits until the follow block is done plus 500 ms,
   so a switch is a short black instead; cancelled cleanly when VRR goes off (the next
   setup unmutes)
 - the follow steps 250 ms apart instead of 1 s (the switch-over takes under 2 s);
   no parameter for either
 - every mode by default (vrr_any_mode=1)
 - the 2-second frame-interval log (test 21) only with hdmi.vrr_measure=1
